<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<Title>TestFramework.Core</Title>
		<Authors>DeadMoon0</Authors>
		<Product>TestFramework</Product>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageTags>Test;UnitTest;IntegrationTest;Framework;Fluent;Timeline</PackageTags>
		<PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<Description>The core package of the TestFramework ecosystem for building integration-style and end-to-end test workflows. Provides the timeline engine for steps, events, variables, artifacts, retries, timeouts, and assertions, and serves as the foundation for extension packages like Azure, LocalIO, and Simple.</Description>
		<Version>0.7.0</Version>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) DeadMoon0 2026</Copyright>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>BREAKING - pass output.WriteLine to SetupRun instead of an ITestOutputHelper, and use CreateAsync instead of the blocking PersistentEnvironmentContext constructors. BREAKING - renamed: WithTimeOut is WithTimeout, Name(...) is Label(...), Transform takes (from, to, fn), and SetVariable takes a value while SetVariableFrom copies a variable. BREAKING - names are case-sensitive everywhere, public members use overloads instead of optional parameters (rebuild against this version), every exception derives from TimelineFrameworkException, and a run's Stages, Steps and RetryResults are read-only lists. An assertion on a variable that was never set now fails, and so does EnsureRanToCompletion for a step that never ran. New: a fresh environment per run through IRunScopedEnvironmentFactory, RunServices.Owned, VariableStore.SetSecretVariable and StepIOContract.ExclusiveOutput.</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="$(PackageIconSourcePath)">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- Core's own suite, and nobody else. A grant to another package's suite is the same private
		     handshake as a grant to the package: whatever that suite may reach for, every other package's
		     suite may not - and it hides that a surface is missing. Config's suite never used one, and
		     Simple's hand-built the run's pieces until RunContext.Detached existed to hand them over. -->
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Core.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.4" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="README.md">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
